{
  "id": "taste-system",
  "term": "taste system",
  "definition": "The taste system is the sensory system for gustation, including peripheral structures such as taste epithelium, gustatory papillae, taste buds, and the neurons and axons that connect them to the brain. It is characterized by specialized anatomy and function and develops through coordinated molecular signals that guide the formation, growth, and targeting of these cells and connections.",
